- **[B190]**            Conclusivity Is Asserted, Never Measured - Inconclusive Is an Unproven Else-
                        Branch
- **Criticality:**      High; the app renders a conclusivity state it never computed, using inputs
                        it already has in hand. Honesty Protocol §1 (no conclusion before evidence)
                        applied to the conclusivity itself, not just the diagnosis.
- **Location:**         macOS/Sources/SyxxKit/Synthesis/SynthesisEngine.swift:332-340 (the
                        decision), :320 (conflict computed), :323 (ignorance computed), :400
                        (conflict's only consumer); Windows/Syxx.Kit/Synthesis/SynthesisEngine.cs,
                        same branch.
- **Issue:**            [CONFIRMED] There are three conclusivity states - inconclusive, probable,
                        conclusive - and they describe how well one or more diagnoses is supported
                        RELATIVE TO contradictory information. The engine computes both quantities
                        that relationship requires and uses neither to decide the state. `conflict`
                        (Dempster K, the contradiction measure) is computed at :320 and consulted
                        only for referral at :400. `ignorance` (m(Theta), unassigned belief -
                        literally how much is unknown) is computed at :323 and flows only to
                        `Conclusion.uncertainty` and Stage-5 display. The state is instead decided
                        at :332-340 by two unrelated belief thresholds, with `.inconclusive` as the
                        terminal `else`. Nothing measures inconclusivity; it is whatever remains
                        when two other tests fail, so the app asserts a state it never proved.
                        Separately, only two of the three states exist in code at all: there is no
                        `probable`.
- **Cross-ref. Delta:** B191 (the type conflation that permits `.inconclusive` to sit in the
                        diagnosis enum).
- **Fix(es):**          [Fix 1] Define conclusivity as a measured relationship between support (per-
                        diagnosis belief), contradiction (K) and ignorance (m(Theta)), all three
                        already computed. [Fix 2] Add the missing `probable` state. [Fix 3]
                        Thresholds MUST be calibrated against the labeled corpus, not chosen.
                        Shipping invented constants here would reproduce the original defect one
                        layer up: a number presented as measured that nobody measured.

